 "eSIM Provisioning Advisor ⊣ eSIM Provisioning Governor, langgraph-clj
 StateGraph (langgraph.graph, esimprovisioning.operation/build), append-only
 audit ledger (esimprovisioning.store/ledger + append-ledger!, MemStore only at
 R0 -- a Datomic/kotoba-server backend is the next seam and is where
 kotoba-lang/langchain-store becomes a dependency). Compiled StateGraph
 (:intake -> :advise -> :govern -> :decide -+-> :commit / :request-approval ->
 :commit / :hold) with `interrupt-before #{:request-approval}` + in-memory
 checkpointer for real human-in-the-loop resume, proven end-to-end by
 test/esimprovisioning/operation_test.kotoba and the demo runner.

 Six ops, all :effect :propose only: :coverage/report, :euicc/register,
 :profile/download, :profile/lifecycle, :smds/register, :ownership/transfer.
 Three of them (:profile/download, :profile/lifecycle, :ownership/transfer) are
 ABSENT from every phase's :auto set including phase 3 -- a permanent
 structural fact, not a rollout milestone: they change whether a real person's
 line works, and an ownership transfer is the primary SIM-swap fraud path.

 What distinguishes this actor from its siblings: kotoba-lang/esim is the
 single authority for identifier structure (EID / ICCID) and profile
 reachability, and this actor holds NO second copy of those rules. The
 governor recomputes every ground-truth fact through the library and over
 recorded store state, never off the proposal; and the STORE applies the
 outcome the GOVERNOR computed, never the profile vector the advisor claimed.
 This is deliberate: the sibling cloud-itonami-card-issuing reimplemented Luhn
 locally although kotoba.card/luhn-valid? existed, and kept its lifecycle
 allowlist only in its governor so kotoba.card.lifecycle had to be corrected to
 mirror it after the fact (2026-07-30).

 Deliberately absent at R0: a per-jurisdiction spec-basis catalog. The
 analogous thing would be telecom licensing plus GSMA SAS-SM accreditation, but
 seeding it would mean asserting jurisdiction-specific requirements this build
 has not independently verified -- the exact failure cloud-itonami-isic-6120's
 ADR-0002 records. Coverage is reported as zero rather than invented.

 31 tests / 167 assertions green (kbb -M:dev:test), clj-kondo 0 errors 0
 warnings, demo runnable end-to-end offline (kbb -M:dev:run)."
 :itonami.blueprint/adr "2607300300"}
